{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And from Your face I shall hide.</b> It is possible to interpret 'from Your face' as 'from the place of Your Shekhinah' — that is, from the place where one sees the face of the Master, YHWH the Elohim of Israel; and this indicates that the first man settled on Mount Moriah, and there were his descendants. And Scripture says: 'Behold, You have driven me this day from the face of the earth' — the holy earth — 'so that I shall hide from Your face'; for whoever is driven from it is called hidden from His face, because he is under the authority of other elohim. And so David, peace be upon him, mentioned (1 Samuel 26:19): 'for they have driven me out this day from being joined to the inheritance of HaShem, saying, Go, serve other elohim.'" "<b>Or one may say: 'And from Your face I shall hide.'</b> You have decreed upon me that You will hide Your face from me, when You said to me, 'A fugitive and a wanderer you shall be in the earth'; for displacement and exile, whether of an individual or of a nation, indicates the hiding of the face, like one who is not under providence from his Master. And if so, in what can I trust, and where is my hope? Behold, I am abandoned to all.'" "<b>And it shall come to pass that whoever finds me shall slay me.</b> He feared the curse of HaShem, and he knew that those whom He blesses inherit the earth, and those whom He curses are cut off; therefore he feared for his life from stumbling and plague, lest the beasts and wild animals kill him."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:23.300600907Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}